  "body": "Some homes offer a place to live. Others become part of your story.\r\n\r\nPositioned within one of Devonport's most recognised heritage landmarks, this unique residence combines history, lifestyle and future potential in the heart of Devonport.\r\n\r\nOriginally built in 1901 as the home of Lodge Albion, one of Devonport's earliest Masonic Lodges, the building has stood proudly for more than 120 years. Enlarged around 1911 by renowned architect Edward Bartley, it later became a meeting place for local organisations, including the early Devonport RSA. \r\n\r\nToday, the building has been thoughtfully transformed into just three private residences, each tightly held and rarely available.\r\n\r\nSpanning three generous levels, this well-maintained home offers immediate comfort with exciting scope to modernise and create something truly special. \r\n\r\nGenerous living, dining and kitchen space along with two bedrooms and a bathroom occupy the main level, while upstairs provides a second living space flowing to a large deck with stunning harbour and Auckland CBD views, alongside a large master suite with ensuite and walk-in wardrobe.\r\n\r\nSecure gated underground parking with internal access to your apartment, complete with a vehicle turntable, delivers convenience rarely found in homes of this character.\r\n\r\nStep outside and enjoy everything that makes Devonport so desirable. Cafés, restaurants, boutique shopping, cinemas, waterfront beaches and the ferry to Auckland's CBD are all just a short stroll away. Leave the car at home and embrace the ultimate lock-and-leave lifestyle.\r\n\r\nWhether you're searching for a distinctive home, an easy-care lifestyle or a rare opportunity to add value to a landmark property, this residence is unlike anything else on the market.\r\n\r\nA remarkable home. A landmark address. A piece of Devonport history.",
